{:findings
 [{:id :F1,
   :statement
   "There is no checked criterion for hole -> closed. C141 read the checkers and found that `closed-by-record` is assigned from the contract `kind` field alone: contract_lint.clj types every kind=\"closed\" declaration :closed-by-record before authority, binding freshness, fixture shape or result are considered, and holder_check.clj checks only that the owner's final segment reduces to a live registry key. No check reads a record. So the transition is written by whoever edits Holes.lean, and nothing downstream can tell a supported close from an unsupported one.",
   :pointers
   ["futon2 holes/labs/wm-contract/C141-closed-by-record-audit.md:5-30"
    "futon2 checks/contract_lint.clj"
    "futon2 checks/holder_check.clj"]}
  {:id :F2,
   :statement
   "A proven pinned obligation was DEMOTED to a hole in the same commit that proved it. mathlib4 86186c3744 (\"Prove exact recorded ablation minimizers\", 2026-08-31) adds theorem wmRecordedAblationNonDegenerate -- a complete Lean proof of nonDegenerateAblationLaw over the pinned exact-dyadic table -- and in the same diff moves the declaration from mkClosed to mkHole. So \"the pinned instance is proven in Lean\" is demonstrably NOT this contract's close criterion; something else is meant by the evidence obligation, and it is not written down. This is the single fact that decides the audit: the one hole whose declared evidence is fully discharged was deliberately left open by the declaration's author.",
   :pointers
   ["mathlib4 86186c3744"
    "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:217 (the theorem)"
    "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:188 (the predicate, docstring: \"tracks the pinned exact-dyadic ablation instance as an evidence obligation rather than treating definition as discharge\")"]}
  {:id :F3,
   :statement
   "The `falsifier` field means two different things across the 15 holes, and for H3/H4 it names the CONFIRMING observation rather than a falsifying one. On twelve holes the field states what would refute the claim (wmRunsOnce: \"no tick-entry invocation completes with a TickRunRecord\"; findF2Receipted: \"selected pattern lacks receipt\"; dirichletAccumulationImportAbsent, whose docstring says outright \"the claim held open is the ABSENCE\": \"a code path from the tick model's o or mu into R17's concentrations\"). On policyPrecisionIsGammaFromBeta the field reads \"a run record in which tau is set by the beta update from G and pi\" and on policyPosteriorImportsPolicyF \"a run record in which Q(pi) is computed with an F_pi term\" -- each of which would make the named claim TRUE. Both docstrings say \"this is the claim held open\", so the claims are positive and the fields describe their discharge. This matters now rather than in the abstract, because H4's named observation is on persisted record (see :H4 below): under one reading the record closes the hole by witness, under the other it refutes it, and the two dispositions are opposite.",
   :pointers
   ["mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6647-6648"
    "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6650-6651"
    "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6644-6645 (the contrasting ABSENCE wording)"
    "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6869-6870 (the two mkHole rows)"]}
   {:id :F4,
    :statement
    "Four of the pointers inside the H3/H4 hole docstrings no longer resolve to what they claim, and one of the claims they support is now false of the code. This is the U29 defect class (drifted pointers, re-resolved through the generator) occurring INSIDE Holes.lean, which U29's scope -- variable-situation-accounting.edn -- does not cover. Checked line by line against the current tree: policy.clj:242-245 and :242-246, cited by BOTH H3 and H4 as the policy score seam, now land on gap-report, an unrelated helper that enumerates :learn-action-class recommendations; the score expression is selection-scores at policy.clj:157 (\"THE ONE PLACE THE SCORE EXPRESSION IS WRITTEN\"), normalised by softmax-weights at :215. war_machine.clj:4450-4451, cited by H4 as where the Laplace channel F is bound, now lands in an unrelated report-prose block; the binding is free-energy (fe/compute-controller-diagnostics observation) at :5543. war_machine.clj:4452, cited as the :R8 route tag, is likewise stale; the tag is at :5857 and now names futon2.aif.free-energy/compute-prediction-error rather than the compute-variational-free-energy the 2026-08-30 receipt recorded. war_machine.clj:4753, cited as the F's one downstream appearance, lands on an unrelated manifest read. ONE POINTER IN THIS FAMILY STILL HOLDS: selection_gain.clj:187-193, cited by H3, still reads \"the field is ABSENT today, sim-only\" -- so the drift is not uniform and each pointer has to be checked rather than the family re-resolved by offset. AND THE CLAIM MOVED, not just its address: H4's docstring says of the policy score \"there is no F term in it, and no free-energy symbol anywhere in the scoring path\". policy.clj:158 now writes the score as \"ln E(a) - G(a)/tau [- F_pi(a)]\" and :184 takes :f-pi-policy-posterior? and :f-pi-values as options, both landed by RUN9/I2 after the docstring was written. The F_pi term is default-off, so the docstring's sentence is true of the default path and false of the seam -- and the docstring makes no such distinction.",
    :pointers
    ["futon2 src/futon2/aif/policy.clj:157-162 (selection-scores, the current score seam)"
     "futon2 src/futon2/aif/policy.clj:184-190 (the f-pi options arity)"
     "futon2 src/futon2/aif/policy.clj:215-235 (softmax-weights)"
     "futon2 src/futon2/aif/policy.clj:242-246 (gap-report: what the cited range now holds)"
     "futon2 scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:5543 (the Laplace F binding)"
     "futon2 scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:5857 (the :R8 route tag)"
     "futon2 src/futon2/aif/selection_gain.clj:187-193 (the one pointer of the family that still holds)"
     "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6647 (H3 docstring)"
     "mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6650 (H4 docstring)"]}],
